\mainpage GraphMine library implementation

This reference documents the complete GraphMine-owned C++17/CUDA layer: the
canonical graph model, result and status types, public problem classes,
runtime backend interfaces, CUDA adapters, CLI, examples, and tests.

<div class="gm-reference-links">
  <a href="../">Code reference portal</a>
  <a href="../../">High-level guide</a>
  <a href="../research/">Research internals</a>
  <a href="https://github.com/wajidmanzoor/graphMine/tree/main/library">Source on GitHub</a>
</div>

\section gm_start Where to start

- <a href="namespaces.html">Namespaces</a> shows the public `graphmine`
  namespace and adapter-private namespaces.
- <a href="annotated.html">Classes and data structures</a> covers graph input,
  options, outputs, status, provenance, and algorithm objects.
- <a href="functions_func.html">Class methods</a> is the method-by-method index.
- <a href="globals_func.html">Free functions</a> includes host helpers and CUDA
  kernels discovered in implementation units.
- <a href="files.html">Files</a> follows the repository layout and opens an
  annotated source view for every header, `.cpp`, `.cu`, and `.cuh` file.

\section gm_flow Execution flow

Every supported operation follows the same boundary:

1. `graphmine::Graph` validates and preserves the canonical external graph.
2. A problem options object chooses a validated backend and optional outputs.
3. The problem class `supports()` checks graph/profile compatibility.
4. `run()` normalizes the graph and dispatches through an internal backend
   interface.
5. A backend adapter invokes the preserved research implementation, checks and
   materializes requested results, restores external IDs, and returns an
   `ExecutionResult<T>` with provenance and timings.

The public problem classes are in `library/include/graphmine/problems/`.
Backend boundaries and CUDA translation units are in
`library/src/backends/`. Use each function page's definition link,
"References", and "Referenced by" sections to follow a call path.

\section gm_cuda CUDA entries

Doxygen indexes `.cu` and `.cuh` as C++. CUDA qualifiers are removed only for
declaration parsing; the linked source view always shows the exact
`__global__`, `__device__`, `__host__`, launch configuration, synchronization,
and memory-space declarations compiled by GraphMine.

\section gm_scope Scope and provenance

This site separates GraphMine-owned integration code from the preserved
research code. Continue to the
<a href="../research/">research implementation reference</a> for the original
algorithm internals. Backend/version/commit provenance and validation evidence
remain in the
<a href="https://github.com/wajidmanzoor/graphMine/blob/main/graphmine_catalog.json">problem-first catalog</a>.
*/
